#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# parallelogram

#% text
# `parallelogram(p, [v1, v2])`: the parallelogram with corners p, p + v1, p + v1 + v2, p + v2; parallelogram() the one at the origin with v1 = [1, 0], v2 = [1, 1]

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
g = parallelogram([0, 0], [[1, 0], [1, 1]])

#% cell
[area(g), region_centroid(g), region_bounds(g)]
#% output
#= [1, [1, 1/2], [[0, 2], [0, 1]]]

